>Michael Panaretos</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael Panaretos was a Greek official and historian of the Empire of Trebizond in the fourteenth century, who served Emperor Alexios III at court and on embassies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-psellos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-psellos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michael Psellos</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael Psellos was a Byzantine monk, writer, philosopher, historian and imperial courtier who advised several 11th-century emperors.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-shishman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-shishman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michael Shishman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael Shishman was tsar of Bulgaria from 1323 to 1330 and founder of the Shishman dynasty, the last ruling house of medieval Bulgaria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-somare"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-somare.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michael Somare</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael Somare was the founding prime minister of Papua New Guinea.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-the-brave"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-the-brave.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michael the Brave</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael the Brave (Mihai Viteazul) was prince of Wallachia from 1593 to 1601.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-ventris"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-ventris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michael Ventris</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael Ventris was an English architect and amateur linguist who deciphered Linear B, the script of the Mycenaean palaces.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-vickery"><span class="enc-name">Michael Vickery</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael Vickery was an American historian of Cambodia and mainland Southeast Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-viii-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michael VIII Palaiologos</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michael VIII Palaiologos was a Byzantine emperor who reigned from 1259 to 1282 and founded the Palaiologan dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-row-the-boat-ashore"><span class="enc-name">Michael, Row the Boat Ashore</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">&quot;Michael, Row the Boat Ashore&quot; is a traditional spiritual first noted during the American Civil War on St. Helena Island, one of the Sea Islands of South Carolina.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michel-aflaq"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michel-aflaq.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Michel Aflaq</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Michel Aflaq was a Syrian philosopher, sociologist and Arab nationalist, considered by several Ba'athists to be the principal founder of Ba'athist thought.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/michel-colombe"><img class